{
  "notes": "20 modules — 10 FIT + 10 FIGHT (one pair per stage), dual-path campaign (each stage runs as FIT, FIGHT, or BOTH). APPLIES THE ARCADE SESSION STANDARD (specs/27, data/arcade-session-standards.json): FIT modules carry a counted `prescription` (sets x reps/sec + category + tier); stored numbers are the NORMAL 'HERO HUNTER' baseline, the app re-resolves easy/hard from the volume ladder by tier+category. FIGHT modules carry `round_source`, a `canonical_map` (thematic drill -> canonical discipline + move), a per-round `combo_spec` seeding the live combo generator, and a `finishers` block (explosive bodyweight, capped, counting toward the plyo cap). Tier map: T1 stages 1-2, T2 3-5, T3 6-8, T4 9-10 — stage 9 is a DELOAD (doses kept deliberately light, no tier ladder). Fields: plyo {foot_contact_cap,set_reps,rest_sec,min_recovery_between_plyo_h,amplitude} on plyometric work (NEVER above the beginner cap); sprint_session on sprint work (full recovery); striking_rounds/round_len on fight rounds; medball on throw work. Numbers shown are the NORMAL 'HERO HUNTER' baseline; Easy/Hard scale via campaign.difficulty_scaling. SAFETY (from the report + convention): warm up first incl. shoulders/wrists for striking; plyo 60-100 beginner contacts, 48h moderate / 72h high recovery, no back-to-back plyo; train striking for SPEED not max force (one-punch power is not trainable); wrap hands + gloves for bag work, progressive contact, wrist aligned; contrast training advanced-only (Stage 8). Every module opens with a warm-up and stops on any pain flag (esp. wrist/shoulder) or safety stop criterion. Voice guidance (campaign.voice_guidance) speaks every movement, combination, count, and cue aloud — no reading required.",
  "both_rules": {
    "description": "When a stage is run as BOTH (fit + fight combined).",
    "sequencing": "Skill/fight first while fresh, then fit. All 10 Garou stages are single-session dual-path, so BOTH runs fight -> fit back-to-back.",
    "shared_plyo_cap": "The campaign plyo foot-contact cap is counted ACROSS the whole session — fight finishers + fit explosive share it; if combined would exceed it, the fit explosive block trims first.",
    "volume_sanity": "In a BOTH session, fit accessory volume may drop one notch so two full high-volume blocks aren't stacked.",
    "readiness": "A BOTH day is a HARD day: readiness gate applies before starting, and it won't schedule back-to-back with another hard day.",
    "announcer": "States the combined plan up front (e.g. 'Stage 4: Dutch Rhythm. Fight — 4 rounds. Then Fit — Explosive Bodyweight Circuit, 5 workouts.')."
  },
  "modules": [

